# 0034 native-display tools: frame-rate and Genie measurement, flip timeline, per-draw surfaces, re-arm, hang log,
#      ANV push verification harness
#
# Base:  tools/ after 0016 + 0019 + 0027
# Files: new: tools/{genie-fps.m, genie-fps.sh, tl-summ.py, dt-tgt.py, rearm-after-fallback.sh},
#        tools/livelog/{xegfx-livelog.py, com.xegfx.livelog.plist},
#        tools/anv/{ssbo-push-test.c, ptr-push-test.c, diff-test.c, gen_vs.py, mkspv.py, plower.m, shader-stats.py,
#        sweep.py, diff-one.sh, map-test.c, pool-test.c, cum-test.c, minininja.py}
# Apply: patch -p1 < patches/0034-tools-genie-fps-timeline-anv-harness.patch
#
# Measurement (paths follow the scripts/README policy: files next to a script are found from its own location):
#   - genie-fps.m / genie-fps.sh: panel frame rate from the accel's flip counter (debug.xegfxaccel_iop_xe_flips,
#     sampled every 0.5 ms on a thread), so it counts frames that reached the panel, not frames the app drew.
#     (1) steady: a window repaints on every display-link tick for N seconds -> fps and frame-time p50 / p90 / p99 /
#     longest gap; GPU clock while busy (debug.xegfx_gt_act every 10 ms: average, maximum, share at 550 MHz).
#     (2) Genie: the tool minimizes and restores its own window (no Accessibility permission needed) -> per animation
#     duration, flips, fps, longest gap.  genie-fps.sh builds it when needed and appends one line per run to
#     data/fps-history.tsv (minutes since boot, WindowServer uptime, results), to follow a slowdown over time.
#     Usage: tools/genie-fps.sh [steady seconds = 5] [Genie cycles = 4]
#   - tl-summ.py <file>: percentiles of each step of the accel's per-frame flip timeline (sysctl -n
#     debug.nvaccel_iop_xe_tl): gap, queued->pop, pop->mark (the composite), mark->arm, arm->latch, latch->signal,
#     signal->next.
#   - dt-tgt.py <drawtime log> [n]: the draws of a passtime log taken with per-draw timing (XeMTL 0031), ranked by GPU
#     time per command buffer, with the source texture and the render target (scanout framebuffer or other image)
#     when the plugin logs surface IDs.
#
# Boot guard: rearm-after-fallback.sh (run as root) writes back the display gates a claim boot ran with (phase 2,
# trial 1, starts 0, fail 0, expose 1, bootarm 0; trial last) after m4a2-bootguard fell back to IntelFB, backing up
# NVRAM to /Library/XeGfxTrial/rearm-*; it also creates /Library/GPUBundles/.xemtl-no-ssbo-push (ANV pushes off),
# remove that file to keep them on.  For when m3db-arm.sh's preflight refuses only because of pins.
#
# Hang log: livelog/ is a LaunchDaemon (com.xegfx.livelog, runs /usr/local/xegfx/xegfx-livelog.py) that streams the
# XeGfx kexts', CoreDisplay's and the XeMTL plugin's log messages into /var/log/xegfx-live/ (fsynced every 0.25 s, last
# 12 files kept) with a heartbeat line every second carrying the flip and E2 counters, so the tail before a hard hang
# survives the forced reboot.  Diagnostics only.
#
# ANV push verification (anv/, for Mesa 0033; XEGFX_ICD names the ICD json, default the installed one):
#   - ssbo-push-test.c / ptr-push-test.c: render hand-made shaders (mkspv.py) reading NonWritable SSBOs, or constants
#     through the binding-640 table, at aligned and misaligned offsets, with a GPU update inside the command buffer
#     and a robustness bound; check the result and print ANV's statistics.  "ssbo-push-test real <frag.spv>" compiles
#     a captured plugin shader under the plugin's descriptor layout.
#   - plower.m: the plugin's module preparation offline (libxemtl_translate.dylib's buffer-address lowering), to turn
#     WindowServer's cached SPIR-V into what ANV really compiles.
#   - shader-stats.py / sweep.py: which lowered shaders the pushes change, and totals for XEMTL_PTR_PUSH_* settings.
#   - diff-test.c + gen_vs.py + diff-one.sh: render each lowered shader with deterministic inputs (32 storage buffers,
#     the address table with misaligned pointers, sampled and storage images, samplers, the bindless heap) with the
#     pushes off and on and compare the pixels byte for byte (MISALIGN=0/8/16 sets the pointers' misalignment).
#   - map-test.c / pool-test.c / cum-test.c: the largest host-visible allocation that maps now, the plugin's
#     descriptor pool sizes until creation fails, and many maps held at once (per-mapping vs total limits; 0028).
#   - minininja.py <builddir> <target> [-n]: rebuild one target of a meson build.ninja without ninja (recompile what
